{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfd7rbvHKg76kUiRMgooZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote the repaired candidate, `coin_belief_exemplar_cloud`, and it now converges: a full fit gave 0 divergences, R-hat 1.01 and minimum bulk ESS of about 1,750, against admission's limits of 1.05 and 100. The self-check prints `OK`.\n\nIt still fits badly, though. On the smoke fit its ELPD-LOO is about −4,542, roughly 1,000 nats behind the best model (−3,531). Expect it to be pruned at the end of the experiment.\n\n**What I changed and why:** the rejected version had three sets of per-person parameters that trade off against each other: the coin switch-rate belief, decisiveness and guessing rate. The coin belief could also flip the sign of the evidence. That made the model unidentifiable, so the chains never mixed (R-hat 1.53, ESS 7). The mechanism is unchanged: a sequence looks random when it is more similar, flip for flip, to a cloud of sequences an imagined coin would produce than to a few rigid designed patterns. What changed:\n- **Coin belief and guessing rate are now shared** by everyone. Only decisiveness differs by person, set up non-centred, with a tighter prior on how much people vary.\n- **Similarity prior widened.** In a 4-chain test the similarity steepness came out around 64–69, far above the original prior's median of 5. I widened it to median 20 on a broader scale; the result barely moved and the fit stayed converged.\n\n**Things to watch:**\n- **Fitted values:** the believed coin switches about 97–98% of the time, and similarity is steep enough that only near-exact matches count. In practice the model behaves almost like \"how close is this to strict alternation versus to the designed patterns\".\n- **LOO reliability warning:** 2.5–2.8% of trials have Pareto k above 0.5, over the 1% tolerance. That was on the 100-draw smoke fit, so the full fit may be better. If it isn't, the model's PSIS-LOO counts as unreliable: it can't be the exported winner, and it would be retired first if the live set goes over 8.\n- **Not checked:** novelty against the other models.\n\n`hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py` are written in `candidate_2_repair_1/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73787,"cache_read_input_tokens":10102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":73787,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"864f7e33-6d45-4522-ac8d-aaf7330eaba6","uuid":"112aac58-796d-4ced-bed5-f018b2663473","timestamp":"2026-10-02T08:46:54.973Z","request_id":"req_011Cfd7ra5ug4hSVJGvXrs9c"}
